Definition

Auto-wait means Playwright automatically waits for elements to become ready before performing actions.

You usually do NOT need:

Thread.sleep()
many explicit waits
Example
page.locator("#login").click();

Before clicking, Playwright automatically checks:

element exists
visible
enabled
stable
attached to DOM

Then action happens.

Why Auto-Waits are Important

Without waits:

flaky tests happen
timing failures occur

Example:

button loads after API response
Selenium clicks immediately → failure
Playwright waits automatically
Auto-Wait Happens For
Actions
click
fill
type
hover
check
